# Cursor-Chrome — INSTALL THIS (binding)

## If you see these user intents, ACT (do not only document)

- "install this" / "hey install this" / "install it"
- "set this up" / "get this running" / "setup Cursor-Chrome"
- Pasted https://github.com/T3ckfr3ak1/cursor-chrome-public and wants the app

## Exact procedure

1. Open **INSTALL.md** if you need detail; otherwise execute below.
2. **If workspace has `package.json` with name cursor-chrome** (this clone):

```bat
npm run install:agent
```

3. **If workspace is NOT the clone** and user only has the URL — Windows:

```powershell
irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/T3ckfr3ak1/cursor-chrome-public/main/scripts/remote-bootstrap.ps1 | iex
```

Else: `git clone` → `cd` → `npm run install:agent`.

4. **Must verify:** `GET http://127.0.0.1:9222/health` returns `"ok": true`.
5. Reply with: health ok, version, absolute `src/client.js` path, API URL.
6. For browser automation after, follow `docs/THREAD-PROTOCOL.md`.

## Forbidden

- Ending with "you can run npm install" without running it
- Asking "proceed with install?" after the user already said install this
- Stopping after clone without `install:agent` + health
